; =====================================================================================
; JAVASCRIPT PROJECT SETUP STEPS
; =====================================================================================
; 
; HOW TO USE THIS FILE:
; 1. Each [ProjectType] section defines a different project setup
; 2. Steps are pipe-delimited: step|command|directions|input_needed|explanation
; 3. Lines starting with ; are comments (ignored)
; 4. Empty lines are ignored
; 5. Add your own project types by copying a section and modifying
;
; FORMAT:
; step_number|command_to_run|short_directions|what_input_is_needed|detailed_explanation
;
; =====================================================================================

[Vanilla JS Static Site]
; Pure vanilla JS - no Node, just a static site you can serve locally
; Great for learning fundamentals without framework complexity
1|mkdir VanillaStatic && cd VanillaStatic|Create project folder|Folder name|Creates and enters your project directory. The && chains commands together.
2|New-Item index.html -ItemType File|Create HTML file (PowerShell)|None|PowerShell command to create an empty file. In bash, use: touch index.html
3|New-Item main.js -ItemType File|Create JS file (PowerShell)|None|Creates your main JavaScript file where you'll write your code.
4|code .|Open in VS Code|None|Opens the current folder in Visual Studio Code for editing.
5|npx serve .|Start local server|None|Uses npx to run 'serve' package without installing globally. Opens http://localhost:3000

[Node + Express API]
; Basic Node.js Express server - good for APIs and backends
; Express is the most popular Node.js web framework
1|mkdir NodeApi && cd NodeApi|Create project folder|Project name|Creates your API project directory and navigates into it.
2|npm init -y|Initialize package.json|None|Creates default package.json with project metadata. The -y flag accepts all defaults.
3|npm install express|Install Express framework|None|Adds Express.js web framework to your project as a dependency.
4|New-Item index.js -ItemType File|Create entry point|None|Creates the main server file where you'll define your routes and middleware.
5|code .|Open in VS Code|None|Opens folder to add your server code. See explanation for starter code.
6|npm run dev|Start the server|None|Runs the dev script. First add "dev": "node index.js" to package.json scripts section.

[React with Vite]
; Modern React setup using Vite bundler - fast and lightweight
; Vite is much faster than Create React App for development
1|npm create vite@latest my-react-app -- --template react|Create React project|App name|Vite scaffolds a complete React application with all modern tooling configured.
2|cd my-react-app|Enter project directory|None|Navigate into the created project folder where package.json lives.
3|npm install|Install dependencies|None|Downloads all required packages from package.json to node_modules folder.
4|npm run dev|Start development server|None|Launches Vite dev server with hot module replacement (HMR) for instant updates.
5|Open http://localhost:5173/|View in browser|None|Default Vite port is 5173, not 3000 like CRA. Your React app is now running!

[React + TypeScript with Vite]
; React with TypeScript for type safety
; Catches errors at compile time rather than runtime
1|npm create vite@latest my-react-ts-app -- --template react-ts|Create React+TS project|App name|Scaffolds React with TypeScript configuration. Files use .tsx extension.
2|cd my-react-ts-app|Enter project directory|None|Navigate into the created project folder.
3|npm install|Install dependencies|None|Downloads packages including @types for TypeScript type definitions.
4|npm run dev|Start development server|None|Launches dev server with TypeScript compilation. Errors show in terminal.
5|Open http://localhost:5173/|View in browser|None|Your TypeScript React app is now running with full type checking!

[Next.js App]
; Full-stack React framework with server-side rendering
; Great for SEO-friendly sites and full-stack applications
1|npx create-next-app@latest my-next-app|Create Next.js project|App name + options|Interactive wizard asks about TypeScript, Tailwind, ESLint, App Router, etc.
2|cd my-next-app|Enter project directory|None|Navigate into the created project folder.
3|npm run dev|Start development server|None|Launches Next.js dev server with Fast Refresh and server-side rendering.
4|Open http://localhost:3000/|View in browser|None|Next.js uses port 3000 by default. Edit app/page.tsx to see changes!

[Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind]
; Full modern stack with utility-first CSS
; This is the current industry-standard setup for new React projects
1|npm create vite@latest my-vite-tailwind -- --template react-ts|Create Vite+React+TS|App name|Base project with TypeScript support and React configured.
2|cd my-vite-tailwind|Enter project directory|None|Navigate into the project folder.
3|npm install|Install base dependencies|None|Downloads React and TypeScript packages to node_modules.
4|npm install -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer|Install Tailwind|None|Adds Tailwind CSS and its PostCSS dependencies as dev dependencies.
5|npx tailwindcss init -p|Initialize Tailwind config|None|Creates tailwind.config.js and postcss.config.js configuration files.
6|Edit tailwind.config.js content paths|Configure Tailwind scanning|See explanation|Add: content: ['./index.html', './src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}'] - tells Tailwind which files to scan.
7|Edit src/index.css|Add Tailwind directives|None|Replace contents with: @tailwind base; @tailwind components; @tailwind utilities;
8|npm run dev|Start development server|None|Tailwind classes like bg-blue-500 now work in your React components!

[Vanilla TypeScript + Tailwind (No React)]
; TypeScript without React, with Tailwind styling
; Good for learning TS fundamentals or building without framework overhead
1|mkdir vanilla-ts-tailwind && cd vanilla-ts-tailwind|Create project folder|Folder name|Creates your project directory for vanilla TypeScript.
2|npm init -y|Initialize package.json|None|Creates default package.json for managing dependencies.
3|npm install -D typescript vite tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer|Install dev dependencies|None|All tooling as dev dependencies - Vite for bundling, TS for types, Tailwind for styles.
4|npx tsc --init|Create tsconfig.json|None|Initializes TypeScript configuration. Adjust target and module settings as needed.
5|npx tailwindcss init -p|Initialize Tailwind|None|Creates Tailwind and PostCSS configuration files.
6|Create index.html and src/main.ts|Create entry files|None|Create index.html at root, src/main.ts for your TypeScript code.
7|Add "dev": "vite" to package.json scripts|Configure npm script|None|Allows running npm run dev to start the Vite development server.
8|npm run dev|Start Vite dev server|None|Vite serves your vanilla TS + Tailwind project with hot reloading!

[Express + TypeScript API]
; Type-safe backend development with Node.js
; Catches API bugs before runtime with TypeScript
1|mkdir express-ts-api && cd express-ts-api|Create project folder|Folder name|Creates your API project directory.
2|npm init -y|Initialize package.json|None|Creates default package.json for the project.
3|npm install express|Install Express|None|Adds Express.js framework for handling HTTP requests.
4|npm install -D typescript @types/express @types/node ts-node nodemon|Install dev deps|None|TypeScript compiler, type definitions for Express and Node, ts-node for direct execution, nodemon for auto-restart.
5|npx tsc --init|Create tsconfig.json|None|Initializes TypeScript configuration. Set outDir to ./dist.
6|mkdir src && New-Item src/index.ts -ItemType File|Create source structure|None|Create src folder and your main TypeScript server file.
7|Add dev script to package.json|Configure nodemon|None|Add: "dev": "nodemon --exec ts-node src/index.ts" - auto-restarts on file changes.
8|npm run dev|Start development server|None|Your TypeScript Express API is now running with hot reload!

; =====================================================================================
; STARTER CODE TEMPLATES
; =====================================================================================
; Below are reference code snippets for the projects above.
; These are comments and won't be parsed as steps.
; Copy these into your files as starting points.
; =====================================================================================

; --- Express index.js starter code ---
; const express = require('express');
; const app = express();
; const PORT = 3000;
;
; app.use(express.json());
;
; app.get('/api/hello', (req, res) => {
;     res.json({ message: 'Hello from Express!' });
; });
;
; app.listen(PORT, () => {
;     console.log(`Server running at http://localhost:${PORT}`);
; });

; --- TypeScript Express src/index.ts starter code ---
; import express, { Request, Response } from 'express';
;
; const app = express();
; const PORT = 3000;
;
; app.use(express.json());
;
; app.get('/api/hello', (req: Request, res: Response) => {
;     res.json({ message: 'Hello from TypeScript Express!' });
; });
;
; app.listen(PORT, () => {
;     console.log(`Server running at http://localhost:${PORT}`);
; });

; --- Vanilla index.html starter ---
; <!DOCTYPE html>
; <html>
; <head>
;     <meta charset="utf-8" />
;     <title>My App</title>
;     <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
; </head>
; <body>
;     <h1>Hello World!</h1>
;     <script src="main.js"></script>
; </body>
; </html>
